Source: ou-ics
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Office Unbound Build <build@officeunbound.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3, python3-yaml
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ou-ics
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, postgresql (>= 15), sudo, curl, systemd
Recommends: nginx, nftables
Description: Office Unbound Infrastructure Control Server (ICS)
 FastAPI backend, built management console, Alembic migrations and the deployment
 catalog. Python dependencies ship as hash-locked wheels (cp311 and cp312) in
 /usr/share/ou-ics/wheels and are installed into /opt/office-unbound/ics/.venv by
 the postinst with `pip --no-index --require-hashes`: no network access at
 install time. The postinst provisions keys, database roles and env files on
 first install only (never overwritten), takes and verifies a backup before an
 upgrade and refuses to migrate if that backup fails. Rollback is a reinstall of
 the previous version plus `ou-ics-rollback <backup>` (see docs/runbooks/ics-upgrade-rollback.md).
 The TLS front end (nginx, firewall) is configured by bootstrap.sh, not by this package.
